/P 207 0 R
/E (This guide provides a simple, educational approach to raising mealworms while teaching sustainability and food system resilience. It is ideal for schools, families, and urban farms!)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (This guide aims to teach students and educators how to build and manage a mealworm farm to promote circular economy principles, sustainability, and hands-on learning. It supports environmental education through practical insect farming activities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Mealworms \(larvae of Tenebrio molitor\) help close the loop in the circular economy by consuming food waste \(organic scraps\), producing protein-rich biomass \(for animal or human consumption\), creating frass \(a nutrient-rich fertilizer\) and requiring fewer resources than traditional livestock.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Within this manual we describe what is needed to start a mealworm farm, in terms of equipment and tools [trays/crates, feeding substrate \(dry and wet\) sieves etc.], whereas we guide the students and their teachers through the process of running their own mealworm farm [mealworm larvae feeding and harvesting, adult breeding, frass collection etc.]. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
