/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 211 0 R
/E (Imagine a world where nothing is wasted! That's the idea behind something called the Circular Economy.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 211 0 R
/E (Think about it like this:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 211 0 R
/E (       up our planet's precious resources.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1141 0 R
/E (In a circular economy, we "reduce, reuse, and recycle." Instead of throwing things away, we find ways to keep them in use for as long as possible. It's like a big, never-ending loop where resources are used again and again!)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1142 0 R
/E ( In a linear economy, we "take, make, and dispose." We grab resources, make stuff, use it, and then throw it away. This creates a lot of trash and uses )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
