389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 215 0 R
/T (Why four stages with different characteristics? )
/E (Why four stages with different characteristics? )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (This complete metamorphosis is an incredibly clever strategy for beetles! Think about it: the eggs are quite resilient in extreme environmental conditions and so they can survive in any situation. The larva \(like our mealworm\) is a dedicated eating and growing machine. Its whole purpose is to consume as much food as possible to build up energy. The adult beetle, on the other hand, has a completely different job: finding a mate and laying eggs to )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (create the next generation, and often dispersing to new locations. By having such distinct life stages, with different body forms and often different food sources and habitats, the young \(larvae\) don't have to compete directly with the adults for resources. This specialization allows them to be super efficient at different parts of their life, making them one of the most successful groups of insects on Earth! )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 215 0 R
/T (It's a truly efficient way of life!!)
/E (It's a truly efficient way of life!!)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
